[00:00.00]Vincent (Live) - 杜丽莎
[00:03.87]词：Don Mclean
[00:07.75]曲：Don Mclean
[00:11.63]编曲：John laudon
[00:15.50]鼓手：Antonio Serrano.Jr
[00:19.38]吉他：Dodong Fuego
[00:23.26]长笛：Charlie
[00:27.14]Starry starry night
[00:34.83]Paint your palette blue and grey
[00:41.75]Look out on a summer's day
[00:46.03]With eyes that know the darkness in my soul
[00:52.12]Shadows on the hills
[00:58.68]Sketch the trees and the daffodils
[01:05.12]Catch the breeze and the winter chills
[01:10.03]And colors on the snowy linen land
[01:17.84]Now I understand
[01:25.06]What you tried to say to me
[01:30.87]And how you suffered for your sanity
[01:37.27]And how you tried to set them free
[01:41.31]They did not listen
[01:44.19]They did not know how
[01:49.91]Perhaps they'll listen now
[01:57.48]Starry starry night
[02:04.79]Flaming flowers that brightly blaze
[02:11.18]Swirling clouds in violet haze
[02:15.83]Reflect in Vincent's eyes of China blue
[02:21.21]Colors changing hue
[02:27.63]Morning fields of amber grain
[02:34.79]Weathered faces lined in pain
[02:38.95]Are soothed beneath the artist's loving hand
[02:45.05]Now I understand
[02:50.84]What you tried to say to me
[02:56.86]And how you suffered for your sanity
[03:03.03]And how you tried to set them free
[03:07.27]They did not listen
[03:10.76]They did not know how
[03:16.50]Perhaps they'll listen now
[03:21.43]For they could not love you
[03:27.53]But still your love was true
[03:34.53]When no hope was left in sight
[03:38.13]On that starry starry night
[03:42.02]You took your life as lovers often do
[03:47.98]But I could have told you Vincent
[03:52.12]This world was never meant for one
[03:55.47]As beautiful as you
[04:06.26]Starry starry night
[04:13.64]Portraits hung in empty halls
[04:20.06]Frameless heads on
[04:21.71]Nameless walls
[04:24.29]With eyes that watch the world and can't forget
[04:29.74]Like the stranger that you've met
[04:36.51]The ragged men in ragged clothes
[04:43.10]The silver thorn of bloody rose
[04:47.29]Lie crushed and broken on the virgin snow
[04:53.10]Now I think I know
[04:58.97]What you tried to say to me
[05:05.05]And how you suffered for your sanity
[05:11.28]And how you tried to set them free
[05:17.13]They did not listen
[05:20.66]They're not listening still
[05:27.02]Perhaps they never will
